@gigarahul @aslater true, yet do not count Instinct out just because it doesn't own the model layer

look at Jev, for example, much less funded than instinct yet still able to produce something state of the art that has rattled the timeline

also, instinct doesnt need the most capable reasoning models to function, they could easily enough just fine tune a chinese open source

@Jason @Jason It might just be, and this is a big maybe, that a large number of people want more  proof that bitcoin security is not going to break because of some technological advancement in quantum or potentially broken because of some newer/unreleased frontier model like Mytos or some conglomerate of open source models yet to come. 

Hacking it does feel inevitable, sure.. but a lot of people own a lot of bitcoin, and as far as I know, which admittedly isn’t a lot, vinyl is not used as a nearly free medium of exchange in nations where currencies are unstable. El Salvador also didn’t back their currency with LPs, which is part of your argument I think.. I don’t know.. maybe they should have but.. what’s the successor to Bitcoin?

You know what would be good? Have @friedberg interview @maxkeiser …

